# A ball from a canonical 2-limb center (an object, so its limbs are stored) and a radius from the
# program, guarded (rule R3): the empty set when the radius is a NaN or negative (e false), the
# whole line when the center is not finite or the radius is +infinity (f false), and otherwise the
# ball itself (milestone1.md, "Values that enter from the program").
kernel:        ball_make_2
input:         c = c0 c1
input:         r
output:        cw = cw0 cw1
output:        rw
requires:      canonical c
ensures:       makes_ball cw rw from=c,r
min_precision: 1
source:        constructors (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       algorithm: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeMake.v ball_make_2_correct
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   every output is selected after explicit tests of the center and the radius (e, f); makes_ball states what comes out

g   = guard(r)
e   = le(0, g)
a   = abs(c0)
f1  = lt(a, const inf)
f2  = lt(g, const inf)
f   = and(f1, f2)
k0  = select(f, c0, 0)
k1  = select(f, c1, 0)
s   = select(f, g, const inf)
cw0 = select(e, k0, const nan)
cw1 = select(e, k1, const nan)
rw  = select(e, s, const nan)
